  "launchAdvice": "Launch diagnostics and suggestions",
  "serviceConnectionAdvice": "Telemetry ConnectionFailed or Social Overlay STOMP 4004 (Inactive timeout) indicates a connection problem in those services, not proof that the application crashed. If the problem persists, check network access and the service status. These messages alone do not establish the cause or exit status; Atyaf does not change network, TLS or account settings.",
  "recoveredUiAdvice": "The log reports a recovered React #424 rendering error. Recovery was reported, but this does not guarantee that every interface feature works or explain a later exit. Check the actual exit status and subsequent output; no rendering or sandbox flags are added automatically.",
  "lostExitAdvice": "The supervisor was interrupted before recording the exit status. An unavailable exit code does not prove that the application crashed. Old missing codes cannot be recovered from these logs.",
  "certificateAdvice": "Chromium error -202 means the certificate authority is not trusted. Check the failing site’s certificate chain, system trust store and any HTTPS-inspecting proxy. This log does not identify the site. Do not disable certificate verification or import an unverified certificate.",
  "walletAdvice": "The KDE wallet could not be contacted. Check whether KWallet is enabled and available on the host. If you intentionally use an active Secret Service instead, Electron/Chromium profiles can explicitly select it in the profile editor. Changing stores may require signing in again; plaintext storage is not recommended.",
  "desktopHandlerAdvice": "The integer warning comes from xdg-open’s old KDE fallback. Updated Atyaf preserves the host KDE session version. Restart the profile with the updated build to regenerate its desktop handler.",
  "shadps4CliAdvice": "This is shadPS4 CLI usage output, not a system crash report. Versions with Big Picture mode need --big-picture (or -b) to open their interface; launching without arguments can exit with code 255. In the profile editor, use the shadPS4 Big Picture option, then Save and restart. Alternatively, import the separate shadPS4 Qt Launcher for the desktop GUI, or supply a game using --game. Flags depend on the imported version; Atyaf does not add them automatically.",
  "useShadps4BigPicture": "shadPS4: use Big Picture",
  "shadps4BigPictureConfirm": "Add --big-picture to this profile’s arguments? Use only with a shadPS4 CLI version that lists this option in its help. This opens Big Picture mode, not the separate Qt Launcher. Other arguments and profile data are kept; no data migration or automatic launch occurs. Save and restart the profile to apply.",
  "useSecretService": "Electron/Chromium: use Secret Service",
  "secretServiceConfirm": "Add --password-store=gnome-libsecret to this profile’s arguments? Use only with a compatible Electron/Chromium application and an active host Secret Service (such as GNOME Keyring). This changes the encryption backend and may require signing in again. Existing credentials are not migrated or deleted. Save and restart the profile to apply; KWallet and system settings are not changed.",
