  "tauriUnknownPathAdvice": "Tauri could not resolve a path during startup. Missing XDG special-folder definitions can cause this (reproduced with xrevive 0.1.22). Atyaf now supplies private Documents, Downloads and other standard folders for default managed config/data paths. Restart with the updated Atyaf; existing user-dirs.dirs files and custom config/data settings are preserved and may require manual review. This message alone does not identify every unknown-path failure.",
  "profileHelp": "XDG paths are isolated by default; HOME is not changed. Default managed profiles receive private standard user folders without copying personal files; custom config/data paths and existing user-dirs.dirs files are preserved. Use application-specific flags for apps that ignore XDG. Arguments and environment values can use '{config}', '{data}', '{cache}', '{state}', '{temp}', '{home}' and '{profile}'. This is not a security sandbox.",
  "windowControlsHelp": "Default profiles inherit system window buttons for GTK/Electron apps such as VS Code and Antigravity without leaving Wayland or changing data and explicit preferences. Custom paths and GSettings setups stay untouched. X11 below is an optional GTK alternative, not the primary fix for Electron editors.",
